s","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:cc1ec74c1a9558b1ca438876150da526722d41aa280cb243ace6d62214a03005","file":"preprints/Variance-of-the-Random-k-SAT-Hitting-Time-September-27-2026/build/source/sections/replacement-sharpness.tex","line":64,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"4d632786e92bff798e7bbdbfd98fde5a0f290e2d2ae5c96ed2c76034dc588ba9","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Variance-of-the-Random-k-SAT-Hitting-Time-September-27-2026/build/source/sections/replacement-sharpness.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:cc1ec74c1a9558b1ca438876150da526722d41aa280cb243ace6d62214a03005","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Variance-of-the-Random-k-SAT-Hitting-Time-September-27-2026/build/source/sections/replacement-sharpness.tex#L64"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:lifetime-sharp}\nFix an integer \\(k\\ge3\\), and put \\(\\beta=k/(k-1)\\).  For every real\n\\(\\gamma<\\beta\\) and all constants \\(D,A>0\\), there exist arbitrarily\nlarge integers \\(u\\ge k\\) and nonempty sets\n\\(S\\subseteq\\{0,1\\}^u\\) such that\n\\[\n q_1(S)\\ge A u^{-(k-1)},\\qquad\n \\tau_k(S)>Dq_1(S)^{-\\gamma}.\n\\]\nConsequently, the killing-probability exponent \\(\\beta\\) in\nProposition~\\ref{prop:lifetime} cannot be decreased in a bound uniform\nover arbitrary assignment sets,\neven above any fixed multiple of the scale \\(u^{-(k-1)}\\)."}
